https://londonconstructionprogramme.co.uk/services/dynamic-purchasing-systems/', NULL, 'c24ad6cb-238d-4105-9a5d-8005677c6777', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 90000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/5e8f0dcd-3119-4222-8ecb-018207507d64', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Architectural, construction, engineering and inspection services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-05-11', '2026-04-24', 'b8d8b5ccf3d8816f010963f6188df1b538bf3b931371ae69494495abe483f7eb') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('d977a7cc-3845-42d0-a3a2-b2b423eaeb9c', 'ocds-b5fd17-fe3391b8-53aa-4521-8017-35a09b3771d5', 'Repair of Steps from Killacourt to Towan Promenade', 'The works relate to the repair of an existing set of external steps providing access from the Killacourt down to Towan Promenade, Newquay. There are no previous specifications in regards to the steps or how they are constructed. They show visible cracking, chipping, and general deterioration. The approximate dimensions (on site may vary) are 180cm wide and 14cm in height. Depth varies depending on the step and whether it  is a landing to another set of steps or not. There are 86 steps in total however there are approximately 20 with obvious defects. The remainder appear in good condition however it will be for the bidder to make their own assessment to verify this.', NULL, 'c66d92c6-8711-4397-a7e5-b0588fb6650f', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 3000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/f14adb68-bb92-4e6b-bd76-28ab62208ea8', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Building construction work', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-05-08', '2026-04-24', '17c91fe613b6da96180c53fe371a7f3d64e91c706512056e97f589b75353927e') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('cc6df345-ef81-48b4-a02f-5ed6050aa1f8', 'ocds-b5fd17-1e666f2c-45a9-4370-9457-4bcaabdf8d14', 'Supply of Defence Specialist Equipment', 'Unite Procurement UK Limited (part of Unite Holding SE), on behalf of the Ministry of Defence, is seeking suppliers to join the Unite Procurement Platform to support the Supply of Defence Specialist Equipment 
The procurement covers;

1. Crimping Tools 
A specialist handheld crimping tool for use in EOD, demolition, and military engineering roles. The tool is a multi-function device designed for use with Initiated Set Field Engineering (ISFE) components, flash detonators, safety fuze, and detonator cord. Key capabilities include:
•	Crimping of ISFE and flash detonators to safety fuze or detonator cord
•	Integrated firing cable cutting capability
•	Integrated firing cable stripping capability
•	Screwdriver functionality incorporated into the tool design
•	Rectifier functionality incorporated into the tool design
•	Robust, portable, and suitable for operational field use in austere environments

2. Injector Stands
A specialist injector stands for use with in-service EOD disruptor systems. The stand is designed to support rapid deployment and stable operation of disruptors in the field.
Key Functional Requirements:
•	Compatible with all current UK in-service disruptor systems (Note: the Needle disruptor is specifically excluded from compatibility requirements)
•	Provides stable and adjustable support for disruptor positioning during EOD operations
•	Suitable for use across varied terrain and operational environments



The Unite Procurement Platform
(Unite | Simplify indirect procurement with our smarter platform) offers a compliant route to market for UK Public Sector organisations to manage low-value, high-volume procurement.

How to Apply
Interested suppliers should register their interest by contacting Unite Procurement UK Limited and provide details of their product range, modification capabilities, and maintenance services. Further information on the onboarding process for the Unite Procurement Platform will be provided upon expression of interest and can also be found at the link attached.

Unite Procurement UK Limited does not intend to appoint a sole supplier for this requirement. Instead, multiple suppliers may be onboarded to the Unite Procurement Platform to ensure a diverse and competitive supply base, supporting flexibility and choice for the Ministry of Defence and associated organisations.

Suppliers are encouraged to express their interest by the stated closing date to ensure early consideration. However, applications to join the Unite Procurement Platform will be welcome at any time beyond the initial deadline. Unite Procurement UK Limited reserves the right to review and onboard new suppliers on a rolling basis to meet evolving requirements and to maintain a dynamic and responsive supplier network.

For any enquiries an interest, please email defence.support@unite.eu with the subject title ''''TSS 636 Opportunity''''', NULL, 'a72f0b4c-4bdd-4e23-b0c2-07114b402f0b', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 2500000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/4412f6d0-7c3a-415e-8894-faa069287f04', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Individual equipment', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-05-11', '2026-04-27', '9a95053e626fbdcd528a15d07000c180da4793947598ebde2ff899227226bb0a') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('25621876-ea4c-4eb2-ad02-b6bb29b762e7', 'ocds-b5fd17-231db3fe-a842-4f33-a9dc-3075ac506832', 'CCHA Trinity Court Fire Door Replacement Project 2026', 'Castles and Coasts Housing Association (CCHA) wishes to procure the services of a competent contractor to undertake the replacement of 58 fire doors at Trinity Court sheltered housing scheme in Whitehaven, Cumbria, as part of their planned compliance programme. As part of the programme, the replacement works include for the renewal of 30 flat entrance doors, as well as 28 stairwell, cross-corridor, and storeroom fire doors. Due to a pre-identified compartmentation issue, works to 16nr. of the flat entrance doors will require formation of a new fire rated GypWall Shaft and GypCeiling to enclose the existing electric meter cupboards, which will require repositioning of the flat entrance doors.', NULL, '07363c41-a94e-440b-aa31-4920e9c965f4', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 750000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/1840c8a7-88bf-4672-865f-6b9908929806', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Fire doors', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-05-22', '2026-04-27', 'e36438361c1c70af54bd5c5ce7f068970b4323446693d08f9f4f1692dbd393ac') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
