Tenders to be submitted to the Clerk''s Office, The Almonry, High Street, Battle, TN33 0EA or via email clerk@battletowncouncil.gov.uk', NULL, 'b4ec90bc-a384-4133-a839-1ef6cd2a920d', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 80000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/5050e681-0b1e-4193-b889-f8ca43261b09', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Electrical equipment and apparatus', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-30', '2026-06-11', 'e24b260633c6672ea5a43dc8988538c4489dfc70fde06787862544b4d4e0fce8') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('ec19e886-5250-4e05-a914-fe53f5e54ae8', 'ocds-b5fd17-1c5ddefe-3190-4397-8b3d-0ec94889b4e6', 'The Jobs Guarantee - RFP', 'Fedcap is exploring the opportunity to deliver the National Jobs Guarantee Scheme Grant released by the Department for Work and Pensions (DWP).
The Jobs Guarantee is a national employment programme designed to support young people aged 18-24 who have been unemployed and claiming Universal Credit for 18 months or more. It aims to break the cycle of long-term unemployment by offering every eligible participant a guaranteed, fully funded six month paid job, alongside tailored support to help them succeed and progress.

Delivered by specialist Delivery Partners, the programme focuses on an employment-first approach, where young people move quickly into real jobs rather than extended pre-employment training. Partners work closely with local employers to source suitable roles -funded for up to 25 hours per week at the relevant minimum wage - and match participants based on their skills, interests, and needs.', NULL, 'ce4cba8d-c798-4311-9ff9-328e3a6c9d62', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/79a70e13-efad-498e-b38a-bd4338e9ec5a', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Education and training services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-22', '2026-06-12', 'cc09263bee17b27a60b463639c78155f275863f8710ed42cabd0e2f8ffbac6ba') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('afeefc71-2876-4fa8-ac69-29a883985750', 'ocds-b5fd17-41843a66-db58-415b-8308-55f2f305c4b1', 'Procurement of firefighting equipment and fire safety measures', 'Partnership Fund for a Resilient Ukraine Phase 2 (PFRU-2) is a multi-year, multi-donor-funded programme managed by the UK''s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office.
As part of its project activities, PFRU-2 is seeking an organization to supply the firefighting equipment and fire safety measures.

Please note the following important tender provisions:
•	the deadline for submitting proposals is June 26, 2026, at 15:00 Kyiv time;
•	all questions regarding the tender conditions must be submitted no later than June 18, 2026, at 18:00 Kyiv time;
•	Price proposals must be submitted either in Ukrainian or English;
•	All tender-related communication must be conducted exclusively in writing via email at pfruprocurement@chemonics.com;
•	The PFRU-2 project is exempt from taxes, fees, and VAT in the partner country. Therefore, PFRU-2 will make payments for services excluding VAT;
•	Email for submitting proposals: pfruprocurement@chemonics.com;
•	When sending proposals or inquiries via email, it is mandatory to include the tender number PFRU2-2025-634.1 in the email subject line.

Proposal Submission Instructions:

ITT_PFRU2-2025-634.1 - review the tender conditions;
Volume 3_Terms of Reference - complete the document and sign the original scan/convert to PDF and sign electronically and submit the completed Excel file and the signed document as part of the proposal.
Annex 1 - complete either the English or Ukrainian version and sign the original or scan/convert to PDF and sign electronically and include it in the proposal submission.

Tenderers are permitted to submit partial offers for a volume less than the total requested amount. Chemonics reserves the right to split the final award among multiple suppliers to fulfill the demand.

Registration documents that follow the laws of your country must be part of the proposal.', NULL, '5cbb1e9d-3c13-4a06-90e6-6489de48f97f', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/c82cb089-1961-4ec8-a977-097a08a8ff48', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Firefighting, rescue and safety equipment', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-26', '2026-06-12', 'db2f7fde1643e1f1ecdac99d75698e6e16278c57359204511cd00552d7e396bc') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('1c5facc8-656a-45e6-a7a0-0b9ce57fb012', 'ocds-b5fd17-4a77cfa2-b5bb-4238-95c4-1272c24085c8', 'Procurement of Semi-trailer low-loader', 'Partnership Fund for a Resilient Ukraine Phase 2 (PFRU-2) is a multi-year, multi-donor-funded programme managed by the UK''s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office.

As part of its project activities, PFRU-2 is seeking an organization to supply a Semi-trailer low-loader.', NULL, '5cbb1e9d-3c13-4a06-90e6-6489de48f97f', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/ed5556d0-8ab7-4061-bf6f-98a205f06b3f', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Vehicle bodies, trailers or semi-trailers', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-29', '2026-06-12', '1ac4b92b5736b2d9e9cbf2e56dd7d4017147228eedaea0a552042ef0731137bd') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('93176f53-529e-452a-9145-ec80ec58dec1', 'ocds-b5fd17-634b93aa-7261-4c65-bf44-89b45545db18', 'Harlington School Cleaning Tender 2026 (Hayes)', 'The Harlington School is seeking to appoint a professional, experienced, and suitably qualified cleaning contractor to deliver a high-quality cleaning service across its premises. The successful contractor will demonstrate a proven track record in educational environments, strong supervisory capability, and a commitment to maintaining safe, hygienic, and welcoming facilities for students, staff, and visitors.

Through this tender process, the Harlington School aims to enhance current service standards by partnering with a contractor who shares its commitment to excellence, reliability, and continuous improvement. The appointed provider will be expected to implement robust quality assurance systems, responsive management practices, and environmentally responsible cleaning methods to ensure the School''s high standards are consistently achieved and maintained.

This advertised opportunity is 3+1 years.

To access the tender pack, please contact our procurement consultant Mr. Mike Newell at mnewell@procurementforschools.com

UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO CONTACT THE SCHOOL DIRECTLY, THIS IS DUE TO OUR SAFEGUARDING POLICY. PLEASE CONTACT OUR CONSULTANT.

Additional information: To access the tender pack, please contact our procurement consultant Mr. Mike Newell at mnewell@procurementforschools.com', NULL, '269a3363-9a9e-4f2d-b94c-274d1447a9a9', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 500000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/d218c2e5-bb0f-4a2e-8882-01c04534c459', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['School cleaning services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-26', '2026-06-12', '058615ca4912cc8651dc75036434ae5e12bee1bc1c50bc5078b52d54fb35867a') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('883154bc-1edc-41f8-9125-e4f976ab371b', 'ocds-b5fd17-700bbc97-a1a6-44df-8d21-524fb2bff906', 'ePayment System', 'The London Borough of Merton ("the Authority") is seeking to undertake soft market testing to understand suppliers that can provide platform, implementation, maintenance, and support for an ePayments and Income Receipting solution.', NULL, '25fa09db-1a23-43c3-94b7-8f3e39e4d113', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 600000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/aee6f4a2-625f-4a4b-ad38-299902ed5a44', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Financial consultancy, financial transaction processing and clearing-house services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-29', '2026-06-12', '527fa5d4244025766196d8cdf624bed633b1ea35dd0da815125fb68057866b9b') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('1ce609df-49fe-4309-a547-d7cd3800103e', 'ocds-b5fd17-716b371a-f35a-412a-ae5f-a8bfb1160b78', 'Fit out and Alteration Works of Broadford Coastguard Rescue Station (CRS)', 'Requirement is for the design and delivery of a fully operational Coastguard Rescue Station (CRS) to support frontline response capability, staff welfare, and statutory health and safety compliance.
The completed facility must provide fit-for-purpose accommodation and operational infrastructure for Coastguard Rescue Teams, meeting MCA standards and enabling safe, resilient and effective emergency response operations.

Additional information: 
The further competition for this requirement is available on the Department for Transport Sourcing Portal:

https://dft.app.jaggaer.com/ 

To participate in the further competition, you must first register on the portal - you can do this by clicking the grey "click here to register!" button on the link above and following the instructions.

Please note that if you are an existing supplier to the DfT, you may be notified that you already exist within the new system. If this is the case, please email mycommercial@dft.gov.uk with your preferred email address for registration. This will be updated on the system where you will then be able to check and update all your details accurately.

In addition, please note that you will require a DUNS number (Dun and Bradstreet) to register. If you do not know your number access the following link to find yours: https://www.dnb.co.uk/duns-number/lookup.html, click on the D-U-N-S number section. If a DUNS number is not found there is guidance on how to acquire one in the same place.

Should you have any technical issue registering on the system please contact the Jaggaer Helpdesk in the first instance:

Phone: 0800 069 8630

help_uk@jaggaer.com', NULL, '56ec195c-c66a-42b6-974f-303e4413738a', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 250000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/929527f1-190e-4cf4-9695-3dd406ec7001', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Refurbishment work', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-10', '2026-06-12', 'd51a8e021a902f1b882021282e9febfd4391543738e71e96326c09cdef8f1891') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('4d723eb0-b3b7-473b-b670-5acc92f795ce', 'ocds-b5fd17-7e4226a9-90d0-44dc-9e7c-a0633b15c823', 'Boundary Road Playground', 'Boundary Rd playground is a well-used playground located near to Lovel End School on Boundary Rd, Chalfont St Peter.  The current playground consists mostly of ageing wooden equipment with wood chip safety surfacing. Much of the equipment and surfacing is showing signs of wear and is in need of replacement. Although the playground currently contains a limited range of equipment, the Council is seeking to include more exciting play equipment that caters to children between 1 and 12 years of age. 

The work is for the design and redevelopment of Boundary Rd playground. This includes the supply and installation of appropriate groundworks, safety surfacing and play equipment. The contractor is also responsible for the removal of designated existing equipment, as agreed with the Council. All works should comply to the British and European Standard for playground equipment and surfacing BS EN 1176 and BS EN 1177.

The contractor will be responsible for organizing an independent, post-installation RoSPA inspection and sign-off and rectifying any issues identified at their own cost. 

Full tender documentation can be found on the Parish Council website https://www.chalfontstpeter-pc.gov.uk/', NULL, 'df508672-6166-4ce7-af3d-837cdfde4319', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 150000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/0cb3f6bf-025d-4c0e-a896-6d2c7211e410', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Playground equipment', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-08-28', '2026-06-12', 'f682d5882a23751b60e6f06fe75d66cf85e34a92e5423ae309653e3d0854669b') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('80c44959-9368-47bf-88a2-4b9f84b137b8', 'ocds-b5fd17-84e8f2a8-8d5f-4caa-b4ca-478c7ef63899', 'Fire Escape Handrail Replacement and Concrete Repairs Work at Kenworthy House, 98-104 George St, Hull HU1 3DT', 'The works comprise the replacement of the existing handrails to the external fire escape stairwell at Kenworthy House. In addition, the scope includes the cleaning and repair of concrete elements to the stairwell structure, incorporating the treatment of exposed reinforcement with appropriate corrosion inhibitors and the application of a clear anti-carbonation protective coating. All works shall be carried out in accordance with the relevant standards, specifications, and manufacturer''s recommendations.', NULL, 'ffbb341a-934e-4b82-91eb-0a235cfb6c28', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 150000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/cc8a1187-16b3-496c-9004-ead141269671', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Construction work', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-20', '2026-06-12', '6dfe7c2d62aaa866f469069483796a01e234abf9223bae37d9b9edb3f06b86a2') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('ff9e17b0-e43a-4e73-a890-38b16377e3f9', 'ocds-b5fd17-90385884-e067-41c5-894b-b0df68361e7f', 'ENQ1290 - Heritage Impact Assessment - Emerging Local Plan Allocations', 'Derby City Council is seeking to appoint a suitably qualified and experienced consultant to undertake proportionate Heritage Impact Assessment (HIA) of a selection of site allocations included in the emerging Local Plan.

The procurement process adopted by the Council is based on the Procurement Act 2023 (the "Act") and the Procurement Regulations 2024 (the "Regulations".)

The contract is estimated to commence on 17th June 2026 and expire on 26th August 2026.

Please note suppliers wishing to express interest and obtain the documentation must do so by 16:00 on Tuesday 16th June 2026. It is recommended that you express interest and obtain the documentation well before this time to allow sufficient time to prepare and submit a bid.

The deadline for returns is 17:00 on Tuesday 16th June 2026.

Documents are available at www.eastmidstenders.org

Please search for ENQ1290 or DN818596.

Please note: we will only accept expressions of interest through the e-tendering system.

Additional information: Please note suppliers wishing to express interest and obtain the documentation must do so by 16:00 on Tuesday 16th June 2026. It is recommended that you express interest and obtain the documentation well before this time to allow sufficient time to prepare and submit a bid.

The deadline for returns is 17:00 on Tuesday 16th June 2026.

Documents are available at www.eastmidstenders.org

Please search for ENQ1290 or DN818596.

Please note: we will only accept expressions of interest through the e-tendering system.', NULL, '9a1ccec9-d177-4a74-b7d4-099faee42488', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 25000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/3eb4af20-4207-46d9-a9a9-ea9645226133', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Development consultancy services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-16', '2026-06-12', 'c4e946fd71f4665ba9b5ead95f82499628a7fe902d06514bb0fc02ee72c0ae2b') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('95a19005-8714-409a-bc7e-230e87bcd24c', 'ocds-b5fd17-9e3b764d-67b6-4958-b183-75321a2fc509', 'Procurement of water tanks and compact mobile water filtration stations', 'Chemonics Group UK Limited which is implementing the Partnership Fund for a Resilient Ukraine Phase 2 (PFRU-2) Project as part of international technical assistance (hereinafter referred to as Chemonics) invites you to submit a Tender for Procurement of water tanks and compact mobile water filtration stations', NULL, '5cbb1e9d-3c13-4a06-90e6-6489de48f97f', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/c9455384-fa1c-456b-9547-a9ac879974cd', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Water filtration apparatus', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-06-26', '2026-06-12', '6fb2626f2d2b551f0f533b294a6244effa3300764b2755f16cfb9b43217dd5fa') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('e3ee3931-d0ad-4f4c-8f36-d2805e8dc2d9', 'ocds-b5fd17-a9668d70-d418-4ae6-9e78-fac26820796b', 'Dorset Peat Partnership restoration works - Greenlands 2026', 'Site works to restore the headwaters of the Greenlands mire system within the Purbeck Heaths National Nature Reserve, as part of a wider delivery programme led by the Dorset Peatland Partnership. The aim is to secure peat forming habitats, improve peat condition, slow flow rates and maximise Carbon capture within currently degraded mire systems.
This will be achieved using a range of sensitive restoration techniques that are described in more detail in the attached restoration plans and project specifications. Activities include creating peat bunds and in-channel dams, mulching molinia vegetation and sallow tree removal.
Contractors will be chosen based on capacity, capability, relevant experience including of working in sensitive habitats on protected sites, proposed solution and cost.
Full details including of how to apply are in the attached Request for Proposals document.', NULL, '4ba03a4e-d8b4-44f9-b632-a04a9a9ecc7f', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 74000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/eff9c7e3-c6c6-4a7e-9632-af8a47d8e1fe', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Agricultural, farming, fishing, forestry and related products', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-09', '2026-06-12', 'edfa9fb4458b967d0aed07c358bac1d09d9abb915951eef32716aebdff79ff01') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('1df516e3-e81e-4bf7-99f3-2ced6834af92', 'ocds-b5fd17-caf640d6-4219-4f2e-b6ed-b219f7b9899f', 'CA18050 - R9321', 'The Trust is seeking to appoint a suitably qualified and experienced contractor to undertake waterproofing and refurbishment works to the A2 Theatre Roof and B7 Plant Room at St Helier Hospital. The works include roof preparation and repairs, application of a liquid waterproofing membrane system, parapet and flashing repairs, drainage improvements, replacement fire-rated external doors, refurbishment of roof safety railings, and waterproof tanking of the B7 plant room floor. The works shall be undertaken within a live healthcare environment and include provision of all associated access, health and safety measures, infection prevention controls, testing, certification, warranties and handover documentation

To access this competition: 

Registered:
Login to https://suppliers.multiquote.com and view the opportunity CA18050.

Not registered:
Visit https://suppliers.multiquote.com then register and quote CA18050 as the reason for registration. 

 Any queries please contact MultiQuote on 020 3920 8054.', NULL, 'faff1f7f-9f80-465d-88d4-8fa9b9abeaca', (SELECT id FROM project_categories WHERE name = 'Enterprise Software'), 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 300000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/4dfaa0c8-fa15-4db5-b9ab-d6bf10682fea', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Construction work', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-10', '2026-06-12', '3babe308e463c969ef9efb02b04bdb9c6edd37e1f7c32841d4bdd4f150cbb68a') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
