INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('467f6a5a-da4f-4627-b535-96020d9ec82c', 'ocds-b5fd17-872707ff-5e36-43cb-8606-57d9cf1a238d', 'Rydal Mount - Brief for a Feasibility Study', 'The Wordsworth Trust invites applications to tender for a feasibility study to identify a future operating model for Rydal Mount, a heritage property located within the Lake District World Heritage Site. Rydal Mount, the Wordsworths'' family home from 1813, was acquired by the Wordsworth Trust in March 2026 with the support of The Julia Rausing Trust and the Charlotte Aitken Trust.

The purpose of the feasibility study is to identify a preferred option for the future use and sustainable operation of Rydal Mount within the broader activities of the Wordsworth Trust. It will consider how continued public access can be ensured, how the ambitions of the Wordsworth Trust and its partners can be advanced, and how the property can be operated in a financially sustainable way that supports the long-term resilience of the Wordsworth Trust as a whole.

The feasibility study will support strategic decision-making by the Wordsworth Trust''s trustees and senior leadership team, and it will advance relationships with funders, partners, and other stakeholders. Balancing experimentation with income generation, this is an exciting opportunity to explore a radically different approach to the management and operation of a heritage property in the 21st century.

The guide price for this contract is £60,000 including VAT and all expenses.

Please submit your proposal by 9am on Friday 24 July (BST) to k.welland@wordsworth.org.uk.

Interviews will take place at Wordsworth Grasmere in the week beginning 10 August 2026.

Our deadline for completion is the week ending 15 January 2027.', NULL, '7ce13c89-208b-4b3c-8510-2bc9670d17e2', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 60000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/9ac26b36-45f1-4314-b411-6da57e4c3676', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Library, archives, museums and other cultural services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-24', '2026-07-20', '30b51202ee2958fce03b7f685ab606e0578edabf04328a47ada7e4b70016252b') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('77224131-0c05-4997-9ea9-4df1933bfd87', 'ocds-b5fd17-897ccb76-e9d2-48f9-b386-111335f7bc54', 'RA359362 - Occupational Health', 'Please see specification below. Please contact lewis.atkinson@londonenergyltd.com with any proposals or clarifications. 

i.	LondonEnergy Ltd ("LEL") is seeking to appoint a suitable qualified and experienced Occupational Health ("OH") provider to deliver a comprehensive, responsive and proactive Occupational Health Service to support the health, wellbeing and attendance management of our 350+ workforce.

The appointed provider will work in partnership with LEL to deliver high-quality occupational health services that support employee wellbeing, promote fitness for work, facilitate effective case management and assist the organisation in meeting its legal and statutory obligations under relevant health and safety and employment legislation.

LEL employs a diverse workforce operating across office-based, operational and engineering environments, with employees undertaking a range of safety-critical and physically demanding roles. As such, the Occupational Health Service must be capable of providing timely, pragmatic and evidence-based advice to managers, employees and the Human Resources team.

The successful provider will be expected to deliver a modern, flexible and customer-focused service incorporating both remote and face-to-face appointments where appropriate, supported by secure digital systems, robust management information and effective account management.

ii.	General
•	Ability to book face-to-face OH appointments where the case would benefit from a face-to-face appt.
•	Local clinic or local hub where face-to-face appointments can be held located close to Eco Park, Tottenham Hale or Liverpool Street. 
•	Ability to book urgent OH appointments and not just rely on cancellations being available to do so.
•	Regular meetings with our client relationship manager.
•	Ability to have a case conference call with the OH doctor, if possible, for complex cases.      
•	Supply of useful data to us by OH provider on a quarterly basis to feed into the Board Report.
•	User friendly OH portal to make referrals on and then be able to see the reports on and historical reports for employees too.    

iii.	Technology
•	Secure online portal
•	Ability to communicate directly with physician 
•	Ability to integrate with HR systems in future / API''s
•	Electronic referral and reporting

iv.	Data and Reporting

Our existing providers ability to pull any data/reporting is non-existent. Would like to see a secure portal and understand what management information can be provided on a month basis i.e.
•	Referral volumes
•	Referral reasons
•	Department trends
•	Absence hotspots
•	Safety Critical roles
•	Drivers
•	Shift work


v.	Additional Services
•	Ergonomic assessments
•	Manager training
•	Health/wellbeing initiatives
 - To access this competition: login to https://suppliers.multiquote.com and view the opportunity RA359362. Not registered on MultiQuote - visit https://suppliers.multiquote.com then register and quote RA359362 as the reason for registration. Any queries please contact MultiQuote on 0151 482 9230.', NULL, '4bc093fc-23b2-499d-b869-07543183acc7', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/376884b7-36dc-4e75-95f2-e35f4bb9755a', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Business services: law, marketing, consulting, recruitment, printing and security', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-31', '2026-07-20', 'e885fa48d62cfc085d98225aaca65f6d5810c11f98d5d96b835b000ae5a20c4d') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('df3025c5-7e11-4fe9-b3c4-6ea222e3a532', 'ocds-b5fd17-aa670c47-2482-4489-ae80-f8cd195d4ffb', 'Project Tullie Phase 3: Gallery Brand Identity Design RfQ', 'Tullie is seeking an agency to develop a distinct visual identity and communications brand for our new ''Active Gallery'' space; where on-gallery activity and collections storage will blend, as part of Project Tullie Phase 3: Breaking Down Barriers.

Full details can be found at: https://tullie.org.uk/project-tullie-phase-3-gallery-brand-identity/

Additional information: Tullie is seeking an agency to develop a distinct visual identity and communications brand for our new ''Active Gallery'' space; where on-gallery activity and collections storage will blend, as part of Project Tullie Phase 3: Breaking Down Barriers.

Full details can be found at: https://tullie.org.uk/project-tullie-phase-3-gallery-brand-identity/', NULL, '4e51eafa-6019-4afd-9e20-a663beffc294', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/3ba15e1d-4b5d-487b-bfcf-bb9d18d96afe', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Advertising and marketing services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-08-24', '2026-07-20', '70bb56e823d4d3a7d513a2bdfc4a87a3c26a0d8264bdb9fb362a36ceef080b3a') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('3aab45f4-b0ed-47a0-b775-ab7070821ea5', 'ocds-b5fd17-aad9c8d1-1d4a-4b31-8816-23c444a1b1dc', 'FSF Dynamic Purchasing System 2 For the Provision of Work Focused Activities', 'The Department for Work and Pensions (DWP) established a Dynamic Purchasing System (DPS) to procure Work Focused Activities for Jobcentre Plus Districts in England, Scotland and Wales via the previous DWP eProcurement Solution (ePS).

DWP has now migrated to a new ePS, Atamis and DWP are therefore reissuing this notice via the Atamis portal. However, please note that ''online'' applications to join the FSF DPS 2 via the Atamis Portal are currently suspended and a temporary ''offline'' process is in place, further details are below.

The DPS is for the procurement of social and other services referred to in Regulation 74 of the Public Contracts Regulations (2015) and as such, the intention is to use a light touch regime, rather than the full regime described in Regulation 34 (Dynamic Purchasing System). The DPS is for the sole use of DWP.

The Flexible Support Fund Dynamic Purchasing System 2 - For the Provision of Work Focused Activities (FSF DPS 2) is the replacement for the DWP Dynamic Purchasing System for provision of work-focused activities known as the Flexible Support Fund DPS (FSF DPS). The FSF DPS expired on 31 October 2021 and was replaced by the FSF DPS 2 with effect from 1 November 2021.

Currently the ''online'' application process is suspended, and a temporary ''offline'' process is in operation. Any new supplier wishing to apply to join the FSF DPS 2 should send an email to cdfsf.adhocprocurement@dwp.gov.uk requesting to apply to join the FSF DPS 2, and the relevant information will be sent to you via email.

Although DWP are currently operating an ''offline'' process to join the FSF DPS 2, suppliers will still be required to create an account on Atamis. Suppliers can do this via the link below, which will take you to the DWP Atamis landing page. To ensure that the page functions correctly, you must accept browser cookies

https://dwp2.my.site.com/s/Welcome

From this landing page, new suppliers will be able to create an Atamis account by selecting the "Supplier Registration Here" button and following the on screen instructions. 

The landing page also has a link to the Supplier Portal Help page, where you will find an article to help with registering for an account

https://suppliersupport.atamis.co.uk/hc/en-gb/articles/4613254620319-Registering-with-a-Supplier-Portal

Estimated overall value of this DPS will be £250,000,000.00


Additional Information
As of 1 January 2021, the internationally comparable regional geography for the UK is the International Territorial Levels (ITLs) geography.

This has replaced the Nomenclature of territorial units for statistics (NUTS) geographies for the UK that were operational when the UK was a member of the European Union. Please refer to the spreadsheet to see how the NUTS Code correspond to the ITL Codes at Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3.', NULL, 'c8eb0cda-6eb8-464d-8aa0-1463c82924c9', (SELECT id FROM project_categories WHERE name = 'Web Development'), 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/22fe743a-bde5-42d7-a284-e0d3a4eb72f2', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Education and training services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2029-02-23', '2026-07-20', '982332dd5ac863966a80bb18d09e48fd710a3b751a75dae95ffd99bd7acc17a0') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('d5791ec4-d5b3-4b2a-989b-de8058832a50', 'ocds-b5fd17-03e8fa8b-be22-4b14-a437-c9e8c97692b1', 'Opportunity to Tender - Civils - Regional Framework Lots (England) - J. Murphy & Sons copy', 'J. Murphy & Sons invites expressions of interest from experienced track matting suppliers / subcontractor for inclusion on a framework of regional lots across England, supporting major infrastructure programmes.
The framework will provide opportunities to supply and install temporary access solutions on a call off basis, aligned to project locations and regional delivery teams.

Project Portfolio Includes:
Network Rail CP7
TransPennine Route Upgrade (TRU)
Peel Ports
Other rail and infrastructure projects across England

Scope of Services:
General civil engineering works
Earthworks, drainage and foundations
Concrete works and structures
Minor and major civils packages
Planned and reactive works

How to Apply:
Suppliers must express interest through CompeteFor to receive further tender information, including lot structure and next steps.


About the buyer''s selection process:
Regional Approach:
The framework will be structured into regional lots within England, allowing suppliers to tender for one or more regions based on capability, capacity and local presence.
Suitable For:

Civils contractors with infrastructure experience
SMEs and regional contractors encouraged
Strong health, safety, environmental and quality performance
Ability to deliver within live and constrained environments', NULL, 'c298cefe-d98e-43a7-b9a2-0c900da44efb', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1000000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/c84e435f-579c-4737-8baf-241798640e1c', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Civil engineering support services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-21', '2026-07-21', '89a2f7f9171859a3b8e8b0ee2df973243faed326be1470e34e06d1d0575bc80b') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO projects (id, reference_number, title, description, ai_summary, organization_id, category_id, source_id, country, state, budget_usd, currency, project_type, status, eligibility, official_link, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, tags, deadline, publication_date, source_hash) VALUES ('7cab8333-882c-423d-9cd7-c4dba8d13851', 'ocds-b5fd17-12709234-d8d3-4c10-8a06-cc62d42219da', 'Opportunity to Tender - Scaffolding - Regional Framework Lots (England) - J. Murphy & Sons', 'J. Murphy & Sons invites expressions of interest from experienced civil engineering subcontractors for inclusion on a framework of regional lots across England, supporting major infrastructure programmes.
The framework will provide call off opportunities aligned to regional delivery teams and project locations.

Project Portfolio Includes:
Network Rail CP7
TransPennine Route Upgrade (TRU)
Peel Ports
Other rail and infrastructure projects across England

Scope of Services:
The framework will cover the provision of scaffolding supply, installation and associated services, including:
Scaffolding Design & Engineering
Design of scaffolding solutions to meet project specific requirements
Provision of temporary works designs and calculations where required
Development of safe systems for access, support and protection

Scaffolding Supply & Installation
Erection, alteration and dismantling of scaffolding structures
Provision of a range of scaffold types, including:
Independent scaffolds
Birdcage scaffolds
Cantilever scaffolds
Mobile towers
Access scaffolds for structures and infrastructure assets
Installation of edge protection, handrails, ladders and safe access systems

Inspection, Maintenance & Compliance
Statutory scaffold inspections in accordance with regulations (e.g. Working at Height Regulations)
Ongoing maintenance, adjustments and safety checks
Tagging and certification of scaffolding structures

Specialist & Complex Access Solutions
Scaffolding for restricted, complex or high risk environments, including:
Rail, highways and infrastructure corridors
Confined or live operational sites
Integration with other access methods (e.g. rope access where required)

Temporary Works & Ancillary Items
Provision of temporary structures such as:
Temporary roofs and encapsulation systems
Hoardings and site protection measures
Debris netting and containment systems

Planned & Reactive Services
Planned scaffolding works aligned to project programmes
Emergency and reactive call outs to support urgent access and safety requirements


How to Apply:
Suppliers must express interest through CompeteFor to receive further tender information, including lot structure and next steps.', NULL, 'c298cefe-d98e-43a7-b9a2-0c900da44efb', NULL, 'b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'United Kingdom', NULL, 1000000, 'GBP', 'Public Tender', 'Open', NULL, 'https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/922d7388-9fcb-4087-aa20-79a17e4b93af', NULL, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Civil engineering support services', 'UK', 'Contracts Finder'], '2026-07-21', '2026-07-21', 'c71de7b5d9d82ae82ed0f1d27fc783608f064266b78fd8184612c51cbd6f7694') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
